<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kovin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Keve</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kovin is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>. Known in Hungarian as Keve, it was a medieval fortress and the seat of Keve county in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, guarding a Danube crossing towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a> names it as the stronghold of the duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glad">Glad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kovin.jpg" alt="Kovin" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. JustUser assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SrpskaCrkva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
